{
  "_comment": [
    "Phase 4 comparison scenarios (phase4-design.md §4.1).",
    "",
    "Each scenario runs on BOTH sides with the SAME user turns:",
    "  legacy side — python-impl's real evals/ stack (DeterministicEvalLLM drives routing).",
    "  pi side     — Faux provider, with `pi_scripted_calls` standing in for the model's",
    "                decision. The pi side therefore measures the HARNESS's handling of a",
    "                given decision, NOT a real model's decision quality. See report §6.",
    "",
    "Phase 10 §③: `pi_scripted_calls` arguments are BUSINESS PARAMETERS ONLY. The",
    "contains no write tool, matching the user's actual intent. The `adversarial` group",
    "deliberately scripts a write the user never asked for; those prove containment and",
    "are excluded from the gate by construction (they are not a model's choices).",
    "",
    "Phase 10 §③: `pi_scripted_calls` arguments are BUSINESS PARAMETERS ONLY. Fields",
    "the runtime owns (user_id, client_request_id, request_payload_hash) are no longer",
    "declared on the model-visible schema, so scripting them would now be rejected",
    "before the call is made. The scenario account is still user_002 — the runtime",
    "binds it from the service claims (see tests/phase2-tools.test.ts P2-2b)."
  ],
